                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] Experienced on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers. Spoiler-free Review. [/h1]\n\nSo this is a ~ 12 minute walking simulator / narrative story-driven experience for VR. The story was confusing for me until the end, where it all came to a gripping conclusion. I liked the Abbott's book demo and this carries that world and story forward. I think this is an overall better experience than the original demo.\n\nIt's not for everyone though. There really isn't a whole lot to do. Interactions are very limited. There are some very very light puzzle elements. I almost hesitate to call them puzzles, it's more like things to make the story interactive versus real puzzles. Busy work. However, the world is so dark and mysterious and the story is intriguing enough so that you push onward and below into the depths. And you don't mind that because you're entering this immersive world. You'll start to wonder what horror awaits you. There's a foreboding sense of catastrophe at the end of this journey. \n\nIs there? I won't tell. All I can say is that it's definitely worth the download. Just don't expect a $30-60 experience when they are giving it away for free. Keep expectations accordingly to the previous free demo and you'll be pleasantly surprised by this free release.\n\nRate 7/10. Devs: please make a full game with this type of theme and just make sure the interactions are more meaningful and you'll have at least one happy future customer here.\n",
